sound at start: on by default, sent at first window focus

Instagram starts its players muted until a volume key, and on a Mac the volume
keys go to the system: stories and highlights played silent. With no choice made
in Visualizar > Som dos Vídeos ao Abrir the default is now "on", and the volume-up
is sent shortly after the first window focus (a muted story creates no audio
track, so the track-started trigger alone never fired). Measured: a highlight
opens its audio with no key pressed.

diff --git a/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm b/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm
--- a/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm
+++ b/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm
@@ -9897,6 +10193,616 @@ @implementation MacApkBackAccessory
 - (void)macapkBack:(id)sender { (void)sender; CocoaDispatchBack(); }
